From: mi5-droidspaces-kernel <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] commoncap: keep the Android AID -> capability mapping

Android does not use file capabilities for most of its networking daemons.
wificond, wpa_supplicant, hostapd, lowi and cnss-daemon are started with
"group ... net_raw net_admin" and no "capabilities" line, and rely on
cap_capable() turning membership of AID_NET_RAW (3004) / AID_NET_ADMIN (3005)
into the matching capability.

That mapping is compiled in only under CONFIG_ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK, which
this kernel turns off so that non-root uids inside a container can create
sockets (net/ipv4/af_inet.c: current_has_network() returns 1).  Turning it off
also removed the mapping, and with it every capability those daemons need:

  wificond: Failed to set uevent socket SO_RCVBUFFORCE option: Operation not permitted
  wificond: Failed to setup synchronous netlink socket
  wificond: main.cpp:130] Check failed: netlink_manager.Start()
  wificond: Fatal signal 6 (SIGABRT)

so the phone booted without WiFi at all (measured on hardware, v1.0.2).

The two checks are independent: keep the container-friendly socket behaviour
and keep the AID mapping, by compiling the mapping unconditionally.

Signed-off-by: mi5-droidspaces-kernel <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 security/commoncap.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/security/commoncap.c
+++ b/security/commoncap.c
@@ -31,9 +31,7 @@
 #include <linux/binfmts.h>
 #include <linux/personality.h>
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK
 #include <linux/android_aid.h>
-#endif
 
 /*
  * If a non-root user executes a setuid-root binary in
@@ -82,12 +80,18 @@
 {
 	struct user_namespace *ns = targ_ns;
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK
+	/*
+	 * Android userspace hands out CAP_NET_RAW and CAP_NET_ADMIN through
+	 * group membership: init .rc files say "group ... net_raw net_admin"
+	 * instead of "capabilities NET_RAW NET_ADMIN", and this is the code
+	 * that turns the group into the capability.  wificond, wpa_supplicant,
+	 * hostapd, lowi and cnss-daemon all depend on it, so it must not
+	 * disappear when CONFIG_ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK is off.
+	 */
 	if (cap == CAP_NET_RAW && in_egroup_p(AID_NET_RAW))
 		return 0;
 	if (cap == CAP_NET_ADMIN && in_egroup_p(AID_NET_ADMIN))
 		return 0;
-#endif
 
 	/* See if cred has the capability in the target user namespace
 	 * by examining the target user namespace and all of the target
